      "created_at": "2018-11-21T21:16:49.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I’ve read in various strategy guides that La Comodora’s card Concordant Helm can allow her to draw an extra card if she chooses to take her draw phase before the play and power phase, since she hasn’t yet used a play or power.</p>\n<p>My gaming group is in disagreement whether this is the correct interpretation of the rule, some argue that since you know you WILL&nbsp;be playinging a card and/or using a power later in your turn, it is incorrect to draw and extra card at the beginning.</p>\n<p>Is there any official rule clarification on how to interpret this effect? I’ve been searching but found nothing that directly confirms&nbsp;how this card should function.</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:52:12.884Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
