      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
      "created_at": "2018-11-23T16:44:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"bluedarky\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bluedarky/48/1975_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> bluedarky:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The rule for drawing two cards during your draw phase is literally “if you have not played a card or used a power before your draw phase you may draw 2 cards.”</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>This sounds nitpicky, but it really does matter; it should be “if you have not played a card or used a power before your draw phase you may draw <em><strong>an additional</strong></em>&nbsp;card” (so that effects that allow an additional card draw during Draw phrase stack).</p>",
